apple finally revealed their iphone 13  lineup but they conveniently left out  many things about the regular iphone 13  and the 13 pro both good things and not  so good now some of these will affect  which iphone model you should buy along  with storage options and accessories you  should go with so make sure to pay  attention as we go through everything we  found about these new phones let's start  with some simple ones the first is a  bummer to me personally and that's the  fact that all of the new iphones are  thicker and heavier this year now the  mini is only five percent heavier and it  was already lightweight so it doesn't  matter that much the regular 13 is six  percent heavier or 10 grams still not  too bad but the iphone 13 pro which was  already heavy now weighs 204 grams or  the same exact as the note 20 ultra  which is much larger with a huge battery  and an s-pen the 13 pro max which was  already a big boy now weighs 240 grams  that's starting to get close to a galaxy  full 3 or an ipad mini 6 and that is  thanks to a thicker stainless steel  frame with bigger batteries and camera  bumps speaking of those bumps apple kept  showing off renders of them but what  they didn't actually mention is that  they are massive and so much larger and  thicker than the iphone 13 camera bumps  which themselves are bigger than the  iphone 12 models these things stick out  so much the apple is now putting rings  on the outside of their cases to protect  the huge lenses so if you're somebody  who hates big bumps or when your phone  rocks back and forth on your desk keep  that in mind on the flip side we have  the notch which for the first time since  its release in the iphone 10 has been  changed apple said it's now 20 smaller  thanks to a reduction in width but what  they conveniently left out is that it is  actually taller than it was before i  knew that something looked off when i  saw it and it reminded me of the hideous  pixel 3xl unibrow but now i know why  let's mention a few positives before we  get into more negatives if you're  somebody that paid an arm and a leg to  replace broken or cracked back glass  apple care can now be used to replace  cracked back glass for only 29  instead of the previous 100 or a massive  599 on the iphone 12 pro max or the 13  for max if you don't have apple care so  make sure to buy that if you're not  going to use the case with that these  new iphones now support dual e sims so  if you'd like you can finally skip using  a sim card at all but don't expect three  separate sims to work along with that it  seems like apple is completely stopping  shipping his iphones with sim cards  altogether along with that even though  apple didn't mention it it does seem  like they are using brand new 5g modems  on these new iphones for two reason the  first being that the whole 13 lineup has  additional bands which also means that  the 13 and the 13 mini have the same  exact data speeds and connectivity as  the pro models but with that we're also  seeing an improvement in battery life  for streaming video which likely means  that this new modem is a 5 nanometer one  like the snapdragon x60 or possibly a  different one instead of the power  hungry x 55 and the iphone 12s but more  on battery life in just a bit and now on  to something that i was extremely  excited about but after digging into  some fine print i am definitely way more  skeptical not as optimistic and that is  the brand new cinematic video mode this  is an absolute breakthrough in video  tech that destroys what samsung has been  doing for years now instead of baking in  this unnatural blur that ruins your  video if it goes off a bit you can  actually apply and adjust the effect in  post you can also select if you wanted  to focus on faces and rack focus  automatically or select the people that  you want to be the main focus and even  change focus between objects you can  also adjust how much blur it adds so it  doesn't look too fake or completely  remove it if the scene doesn't work out  there is nothing out there that matches  this level of control other than a real  camera so it is no wonder that apple  spent so much time on it but there is  just one catch that they didn't mention  and that is the fact that it only works  when shooting 1080p video and only at 30  frames per second now i know why so much  of the video looked soft when they  showed it off and i can't understand why  it's limited to 1080p there's just so  much data that needs to be processed and  of course they do want to upsell you on  the iphone 14 pro which will probably be  able to do it in 4k but it is still a  bummer to go back to 1080p video after  shooting 4k since the iphone 6s yes that  was a while ago apple also confirmed the  long rumored prores recording making the  iphone a more pro video device they  cleverly mentioned that the 13 pro can  shoot pro res meaning the regular 13  can't which is acceptable but they also  snuck in that the 13 pro can shoot  cinematic video or pro res meaning not  both so you either get the cool blur or  less compression artifacts and there is  one more catch if you buy a 128 gig  iphone 13 pro like i always do since i  use icloud they are also limiting that  prores recording to 1080p just like the  cinematic mode man i guess 2021 is the  year of 1080p  if you want to shoot pro res in 4k you  better cough up some extra cash for at  least 256 gigabytes of storage so yes  this is a software limitation just to  save you on storage space now on the  positive side this year thankfully there  are no camera differences between the 13  pro and the 13 pro max like we had last  year so if you like the smaller size or  you want to save 100 bucks and put that  towards extra storage you are not going  to lose out like you did with the iphone  12 pro and with that we will likely have  the biggest camera quality differences  we have ever seen between the regular  and the pro models just take another  look at the size difference of the  camera bumps even though the 13 is  inheriting the iphone 12 pro max's  camera system with the sensor  stabilization and the photos will be  good the pro models are getting massive  updates and they're going to be a lot  better they have new three-time zoom  lenses with night mode capabilities the  much upgraded ultrawide camera that not  only captures a lot more light but can  now take insane macro shots which is not  possible with the iphone 13 or the 13  mini and even though apple finally gave  4k 60 hdr video capture support to the  13 which was just a software limitation  before we still don't have night mode  portrait support which makes a massive  difference in these kinds of low light  shots if you guys want to see an ultra  detailed camera comparison between the  iphone 13 and the 13 pro hit that  subscribe button below and with that you  guys can help us reach our goal of 1  million subscribers we would definitely  appreciate it now as you may have seen  the iphone 13 gained two and a half  hours of battery life compared to the  iphone 12 whereas the 13 pro only gained  one and a half hours now that is because  of the new pro motion display that could  take more power but what apple didn't  specifically mention is that it can also  use less power as well if we look at the  detailed battery life specs you'll see  that when watching video the 13 pro  actually gets three extra hours of video  playback from the device itself or up to  five extra hours when streaming compared  to the iphone 13. now i'm not sure why  there's a bigger difference when  streaming than from local storage maybe  because of the extra graphics being more  efficient but the better battery life is  definitely because of the new promotion  display dropping all the way down to 10  hertz instead of being locked at 60  hertz this means that when you're  watching movies or videos the display  can match 24 or 30 fps to have less  judder and to save battery and the same  thing goes for games this is basically  like g-sync so if you're playing games  at lower frame rates it will feel  smoother and you will save battery so  basically even though apple said the 13  will have better battery it really  depends on what you do so don't buy the  13 just for that and along with that  they also didn't mention the amounts of  ram these phones have the 13 pro still  has 6 gigabytes while the 13 has 4  gigabytes so unfortunately we don't have  any changes but we did get a process  change of course the a15 but apple was  very sly about that they were very vague  in performance stating things like the  fastest processors ever and better than  competition but that is because not that  much of improvement has been made on the  cpu side probably the smallest upgrade  in years only jumping from 4200 up to 4  800 in the pro max models but thankfully  on the graphics side we have really good  improvements at least with the iphone 13  pro models 5 core graphics leaked  geekbench metal scores show 14 200 which  is insane performance upgrade compared  to the iphone 12 pro max's 9000 or close  to 60 percent but if you go for the  iphone 13 that drops all the way down to  10 600 which isn't really worth  upgrading for so if you play games  definitely go for the pro model now the  last discovery is a bit of a funny one  iphones have been able to fast charge to  50 in 30 minutes for many years now but  this year apple didn't mention that this  is no longer the case if you buy the 13  pro max it will now take 35 minutes to  reach 50 percent with a 20 watt power  adapter because that is no longer enough  to charge its bigger battery now sure  the five extra minutes doesn't really  matter but what apple also didn't  mention is that the pro max models can  actually accept more than 20 watts of  charging the 12 for max accepted up to  23 watts so who knows this one might do  25 26 27 we'll test it out once we get  it so if you're buying a fast charger  for your pro max and you want the  fastest speeds pick up at least a 30  watt charger to get the fastest speed  i'll go ahead and link one down below  along with the 21 anchor for just 11  bucks as tiny and as prongs we highly  recommend that one as well so thank you  guys for watching let us know your  thoughts down in the comment section  below click that subscribe button above  to help us reach our goal of 1 million  subscribers we would greatly appreciate  it check out one of those great videos  over there that's been max and i will  see you in the next video  [Music]
 

